From ff03de740b2de10cbba9eaefd4e09beca30a960e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Parada <livercake@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:57:56 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] MUSEUM: ignore packed core artifacts (*-wasm.data)

Packed core .data files are build output, not source. They run to
hundreds of MB each and would swamp the patch history that
arties/GPL-Source-Preservation-Plan.md depends on for Corresponding
Source provenance.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .gitignore | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index bcfc6409bb..07e4e5ab27 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -283,3 +283,8 @@ gfx/drivers/rsx_shaders/modern_opaque.fpo
 gfx/drivers/rsx_shaders/modern_opaque.vpo
 pkg/psl1ght/pkg/USRDIR/shaders_cg/
 !pkg/psl1ght/pkg/USRDIR/system/
+
+# MUSEUM (2026-10-07): packed core artifacts are build output, never source.
+# See arties/GPL-Source-Preservation-Plan.md -- these must never be committed,
+# they are hundreds of MB and would swamp the patch history.
+*-wasm.data
-- 
2.43.0

